## The doc test (`admission-spec-test`)

Per the orchestrator note collab/1792242500000-note-ad1-test-name.txt it
lives in `test/yin/repl/admission_doc_test.cljc`. It is enabled (no
flag). It reads section 7.5 from `### 7.5` to the next heading of level
three or higher (the `####` subsections are included) and returns its
divergences as data: every keyword of `admission/reasons` must appear;
`serve-budget` and `pair-capacity` must be followed by `(64)` and
`(1024)` in parentheses, the form 7.5.4 uses; the literal
`origin + "."` must appear. Verified against master's 7.5 text (a copy
from `git show master:...`): no divergence; and three mutated texts
(a reason renamed, `(64)` to `(65)`, the prefix literal dropped) are each
reported. In this worktree the file has no 7.5, so the test reports
