   645	      and the runner's autorun — so the worker has its own `held`
   646	      registry and shares the process's pid, exactly like a second worker
   647	      in a real process.  Flags (an Int32Array over a SharedArrayBuffer):
   648	      [1|2] loaded, [0] start, [3|4] outcome (1 owns, 2 refused), [5]
   649	      release, [6|7] released.  A refused contender retries with a small
   650	      random pause, as an operator restarting would, so the pair settles
   651	      on exactly one owner."
