29:No session or subject travels in the question; the subject is the interpreter's context (section 6). Direct `:name-env` entries, provenance `:composition`, are not asked. Non-DHT sources have no pair. The link response on allow gains `:yin.admit/id`, `:yin.admit/decision :allow`, `:yin.admit/asserters` and `:yin.admit/address`. A refusal copies into the link refusal shape with the answer's reason and open keys. A malformed answer refuses `:yin.admit/malformed-answer`; non-empty conditions refuse `:yin.admit/unsupported-condition`; both are final for that link. A nil `:admission` on a DHT source refuses `:yin.admit/unconfigured`.
31:## 2. The admission state and the serve round (F1 FIXED, kept)
42:The dht branch of `answer` (link.cljc 392-405) becomes three cases, in this order, replacing the `:admit` call at 397-399:
45:2. **Asked and answered.** An allow runs `(dht-attempt node declared request (:yin.admit/address asked))` with the retained address (`dht-attempt` already takes an explicit address, link.cljc 330), never a fresh `resolve-name`. A refuse is the body. When the response lands, serve drops the asked entry and its answer.
52:**Registry record (P2-4).** `engine/link-install` (engine.cljc 1390) rebuilds the entry through `module/link-module` (module.cljc 88-98), whose fixed map drops the response's admission keys. The edit: after `module-entry` and before `receive-module`, assoc onto the entry an `:admission` map `{:yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision :yin.admit/asserters :yin.admit/address}` copied from the response when it carries `:yin.admit/decision :allow`. `spawn-module` inheritance (engine.cljc 1289-1307) and dependency transfer (1396-1403) copy entries whole minus `:bindings`, so the record is inherited and transferred without further edits. Direct `:name-env` entries carry no `:admission` key.
54:**F1 test.** Publish M1 for `pym.m` under principal B. Import on a reader that declares B but trusts nobody in process, so the question stays open. Publish a new head of B moving `pym.m` to M2 and step the world until the follower installs it. Append an allow for the open admission id. Drive. Assert the response's `:yin.admit/address` is M1's content address, the response's `:manifest` value equals M1's manifest value, the node holds a module record for M1 and none for M2, the installed registry entry and an install child's inherited entry both carry `:admission` with that id and address, and the pending entry's `:admission` id never changed.
65:`base` is `(:base parked)`; `parked` is the VM after `engine/abandon-installs` and the `abandon-link` fold, the `vm` already bound in `abandon-pending` (repl.cljc 1391-1432). `carry-link-identity` (1217-1229) takes the max of the same two counters, so the upper bound is what the base inherits.
84:- **In-drive.** `drive-links` (1296-1351) runs `admission/serve` right after `link/serve`, assocs its `:admission` on the state before `vm/run` (so `link-raise` sees it), and the continuation test at 1340 becomes `(or (:progress? served) (:progress? admitted) (:progress? answered))`. With the in-process interpreter one require costs two extra rounds. With none, the drive ends with the link pending, bounded by `link-round-budget` as today.
92:**P1-2 acceptance (new).** (i) After the initial drive stops, append `serve-budget` answers for unknown ids and then the valid allow; call `recheck-on-answers` alone, at most twice: the require completes, and `:checks` is 0 after the first call. (ii) Gap recovery: a pair built with capacity 4 (`make-pair` gains an optional capacity, default `pair-capacity`); mint the cursor at the oldest end, append six answers for unknown ids then the valid allow; `recheck-on-answers` adopts the recovery cursor on the gap outcome and the require completes within two calls. (iii) `serve-budget` irrelevant answers and no allow, three hook calls: `:checks` stays 0 and the cursor has advanced past all of them.
102:`yin.repl.admission` is composed from `{:trusted #{...} :verify f :decision d :decision-medium m}` and answers with `(verify decision context question)`: nil allows, a reason map refuses. The context is composition-owned, built by `admission/context` from the session: `{:yin.admit/subject "ed25519:<hex>" | nil, :yin.admit/session <shell token now; [id revision] once the REPL F2 slice lands>}`. Authorization vocabulary stays in context and policy; the question and the linker carry none.
106:The decision snapshot is the static `:decision` value, or the newest value on a capacity-1 `:decision-medium`, read once per round. Absent snapshot: no answer, the question stays pending. Ended snapshot: refuse `:yin.admit/decision-ended`. Default policy: `decision` is `#{own principal} ∪ :trusted`, allow when some asserter is in it, else `:yin.admit/untrusted-principal` naming the asserters. Policies compose as verify functions, first reason wins. One interpreter writes the answer medium.
110:**F4 acceptance (executable, AD-1).** A recording `verify` asserts it received exactly the snapshot, the context and the question; absent snapshot leaves the question unanswered after a round and reports no progress; ended snapshot refuses `:yin.admit/decision-ended` with no load started; no key of the question or the link request is `:yin.admit/subject`, `:yin.admit/session` or namespaced `dao.shibi`.
114:Admission governs entry into a session's module registry; the registry follows the session. The cache hit (module.cljc 552-554) answers a require from the registry without a question; install children inherit entries (engine.cljc 1289-1307); parents receive what children installed (1396-1403); `(lang ...)` preserves the registry (repl.cljc 1799, per the review). One allow authorizes every later require of that module in that session; `(reset)` and `(vm ...)` establish a fresh registry and fresh admission state. Untrust changes only later answers. The interpreter sees names, addresses, asserters and provenance, never bytes; the linker and L-e verify closure origin, store ownership, dependency pins and the primitives profile whatever the answer says. Conditions must be empty.
118:- **(a) Python policy.** Delete `principal-admission` from publication.cljc (130-148) with the ruling 19 paragraph of its docstring. The `:admit` option and its paragraph leave `link/composition` (link.cljc 147-153, 166). The default `yin.repl.admission` policy answers `:yin.admit/untrusted-principal`.
119:- **(b) Tests.** `foreign-principals-are-refused-until-l-e-test` (dht_import_test.cljc 111-136) moves to `test/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc` as `an-untrusted-principal-is-refused-by-the-default-interpreter-test`. `foreign-principal-is-refused` (454-474) becomes `an-untrusted-principal-is-refused-on-every-vm`; an allow case trusts B. `run-over-dht` (281-311) mints `(admission/make-state)` beside `make-pair`, passes `:admission` to `link/serve`, runs `admission/serve` on the result with the source's policy, and carries both successors (F5, kept). `source` (314-320) composes `:admission {:trusted #{pa}}`.
121:- **(d) REPL.** `make-session` (732-770) mints the admission state beside the link pair; `create-state` takes `:admission` beside `:link-policy`, defaulting to the own key from `:dht-key`; `drive-links`, `abandon-pending`, `link-raise`, `carry-served`, `recheck-on-answers`, `(trust p)`, `(untrust p)`, `(trusted)`; the `:admission` entry key in `link-install`; `make-pair` optional capacity.
129:- **AD-1 seam.** `yin.repl.admission` with `make-state`, `context`, `serve`, `drain`, `reasons`; admission state through `link/serve`; `link/retire`; `:admit` removed; the `link-install` admission record; `make-session` default state; nil `:admission` refuses `:yin.admit/unconfigured`. Linker engineer. Portable tests in `admission_test.cljc` on hand-made questions and media. Acceptance: a trusted asserter's module imports on every VM with the admission record and address in the installed and inherited registry entries; an untrusted one is refused with no load started; a question append reports progress; an unanswered question survives sixty-four rounds unchanged; a duplicate allow is dropped and the first stands; an answer for an unknown id is consumed and dropped; non-empty conditions refuse `:yin.admit/unsupported-condition`; a malformed answer refuses `:yin.admit/malformed-answer`; `retire` passes P1-1 (i)-(iii); `drain` passes P1-2 (ii) gap recovery at the seam; the F4 executable acceptance; the F1 head-change test.
130:- **AD-2 Python.** (a) and (b). Compiler engineer, coordinated with the yang.python orchestrator through collab. Acceptance: no `:yang.python.antlr/foreign-principal` remains; `run-over-dht` runs both interpreters; the published DHT artifact is unchanged; the F1 test lives here because it needs a second head.
133:Order: AD-1 (with AD-0's test), then AD-2 and AD-3 in either order.
135:**Must not land before L-e.** Anything that claims untrusted-origin imports are safe; a default decision other than own principals; honoring any non-empty condition; a weakening of profile or dependency-pin discharge (linker.cljc 1020-1075) or export-origin validation (engine.cljc 1347-1383); admission on the content pair or in any frontend. The register-VM cutover is unaffected: everything here is AST-level data on streams.
146:- Which head event the follower emits when an installed principal's head moves; the F1 test may need `:confirmed` or `:installed` stepping.
